This project started from the GenVibe Parlo chat-app template (Expo SDK 57, Expo Router; runs in Expo Go on iPhone and Android, and on the web). Read .genvibe/memory.md first.
When the user describes their app, first update constants/content.ts: brand name, palettes, people and portraits, sample chats, stories, pretend replies and copy. Every screen reads from it.
Keep the screens in app/ (Chats, chat/[id], photo, profile, new) and the shared pieces in components/ui; new screens go in app/ as Expo Router routes.
Keep the platform fallbacks: *.ios.tsx files hold Liquid Glass (Glass, GlassGroup); the plain .tsx files are the web versions and *.android.tsx the Android ones. Icons go through components/ui/Icon.tsx with both an SF Symbol and a Material Symbol name.
Never add modules that need a development build (no MMKV, Skia, Nitro modules, expo-dev-client or custom native code). Install Expo packages with `npx expo install`, then run `yarn dev`.
Portraits live in assets/avatars and photos in assets/photos as real JPEG files. Do not set ios.bundleIdentifier or android.package in app.json.
